=== A3.b norm counts ===
r_4(n) = 8 sigma(n) for all odd n <= 400 (direct count on Z^4): True
r_4(n) = 24 sigma(odd part) for even n <= 400: True
Dirichlet convolution (r_2 * r_2)(n) [= norm count on the maximal order Z[i]^2] at 1, 2, 4, 5, 9, 13, 25: [16, 32, 48, 64, 32, 64, 160]
   it vanishes for every n = 3 mod 4, n <= 400: True
   other n <= 60 with (r_2 * r_2)(n) = 0: [6, 12, 14, 21, 22, 24, 28, 30, 33, 38, 42, 44, 46, 48, 54, 56, 57, 60]
sign-table lattice Z<1,i,j,ij> (index 4 in Z[i]^2): norm counts at 1, 2, 4, 5, 9, 13, 25: [8, 0, 16, 32, 16, 32, 80]
   = (r_2 * r_2)(n) / 2 for every odd n <= 400: True
   norm-1 elements (the signed units): 8  (the group C_4 x C_2 has order 8; Z[i]^2 has 16 units)
   even n: (n, sign-table lattice count, Dirichlet convolution): [(2, 0, 32), (4, 16, 48), (8, 0, 64), (10, 0, 128), (16, 16, 80), (20, 64, 192)]

=== A3.c Out(Q_8) on the three axes ===
|Aut(Q_8)| = 24
induced permutations of the axes (i, j, k) -> multiplicity (kernel = Inn): [((1, 2, 3), 4), ((1, 3, 2), 4), ((2, 1, 3), 4), ((2, 3, 1), 4), ((3, 1, 2), 4), ((3, 2, 1), 4)]
action on the cyclic sign triangle 1 -> 2 -> 3 -> 1: [((1, 2, 3), 'automorphism'), ((1, 3, 2), 'anti-automorphism'), ((2, 1, 3), 'anti-automorphism'), ((2, 3, 1), 'automorphism'), ((3, 1, 2), 'automorphism'), ((3, 2, 1), 'anti-automorphism')]
so Aut(Q_8)/Inn = S_3 acts on the axes as Aut+-(C_3): 3 automorphisms, 3 anti-automorphisms: True

=== A3.d the 128 cyclic orientations of the Fano lines ===
(H, alternative, norm multiplicative, doubly regular) -> number of orientations: [((171, False, False, False), 112), ((189, True, True, True), 16)]

=== A3.e 240 labelled Paley tournaments ===
labelled tournaments on 7 vertices with H = 189: 240  (7!/21 = 240)
max H at order 7: 189 ; labelled tournaments with H = 171: 1680
labelled Fano planes on 7 points: 30
(Fano plane, orientation of its lines) pairs giving a Paley tournament: 480 = 30 x 16
distinct labelled Paley tournaments reached: 240 ; each reached [2] times
so 240 = 30 * 16 / 2 = 16 * 15 on the Paley side (15 = pairs of Fano planes sharing the 14 cyclic triangles)
P_7 (QR = 1, 2, 4): cyclic triangles: 14 ; they split into the two Fano planes {0,1,3}+i and {0,2,3}+i: True
|Aut(P_7)| = 21

